[SPEAKER_02]: It doesn't matter.

195
00:12:33,384 --> 00:12:36,425
[SPEAKER_02]: The point is not to go further and get the right solid aspect.

196
00:12:36,445 --> 00:12:42,027
[SPEAKER_02]: The point is to start seeing the right order, the right context of your situation based on that solid aspect.

197
00:12:43,047 --> 00:12:46,569
[SPEAKER_02]: So, again, if I ask you, do you have the body of a certain form?

198
00:12:47,049 --> 00:12:48,409
[SPEAKER_02]: You don't need to stop and think about it.

199
00:12:48,429 --> 00:12:49,050
[SPEAKER_02]: You already know.

200
00:12:49,070 --> 00:12:49,650
[SPEAKER_02]: Yes, of course.

201
00:12:50,685 --> 00:13:06,613
[SPEAKER_02]: So, allow that thought to endure peripherally, while you then see yourself wanting this, not wanting that, thinking this, thinking that, wanting to do this, and so on, within the context of that necessary solid lump that needs to be present there, in order for you to want anything.

202
00:13:09,094 --> 00:13:12,656
[SPEAKER_00]: Seeing that that body, that solid aspect, comes first.

203
00:13:13,396 --> 00:13:13,597
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes.

204
00:13:13,697 --> 00:13:15,097
[SPEAKER_00]: Before microbe, before microbe.

205
00:13:15,137 --> 00:13:20,340
[SPEAKER_02]: It comes first in the sense of it's there as a container of everything you can think, including the solid aspect.

206
00:13:22,761 --> 00:13:23,982
[SPEAKER_02]: So, you can't step outside of it.

207
00:13:24,542 --> 00:13:26,864
[SPEAKER_02]: Inasmuch, you cannot step outside of your body and your senses.

208
00:13:29,666 --> 00:13:30,467
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, you can have...

209
00:13:31,327 --> 00:13:34,790
[SPEAKER_01]: The solid aspect can be there, even if you're not thinking about it.

210
00:13:35,691 --> 00:13:40,394
[SPEAKER_01]: But the thought of the solid aspect is inconceivable without the solid aspect in mind.

211
00:13:40,414 --> 00:13:42,936
[SPEAKER_01]: So, therefore, the solid aspect comes first.

212
00:13:42,956 --> 00:13:44,537
[SPEAKER_01]: That's like... Yeah.

213
00:13:46,739 --> 00:13:48,861
[SPEAKER_02]: And I would stick to this solid aspect, then...

214
00:13:49,641 --> 00:13:51,943
[SPEAKER_02]: If you get the sense of that, then you can refine it to the

215
00:13:53,869 --> 00:13:58,812
[SPEAKER_02]: Water, sort of fluid aspect, or the heat aspect, but they're a bit more refined.

216
00:13:59,773 --> 00:14:01,714
[SPEAKER_02]: And you wouldn't find them left or right from the solid.

217
00:14:01,734 --> 00:14:02,835
[SPEAKER_02]: You find it within the solid.

218
00:14:05,216 --> 00:14:07,077
[SPEAKER_02]: It's not like this one, two, three, four I have to meet.

219
00:14:07,197 --> 00:14:07,357
[SPEAKER_02]: No.

220
00:14:07,438 --> 00:14:08,698
[SPEAKER_02]: You meet one, you met them all.

221
00:14:13,261 --> 00:14:14,582
[SPEAKER_01]: The space one is a bit different.

222
00:14:15,963 --> 00:14:16,163
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

223
00:14:16,663 --> 00:14:18,364
[SPEAKER_02]: But again, it's even more refined.

224
00:14:18,384 --> 00:14:21,326
[SPEAKER_02]: And then the utmost refined one is the consciousness.

225
00:14:23,467 --> 00:14:25,427
[SPEAKER_01]: That's in the suttas about the sīlas.

226
00:14:25,607 --> 00:14:29,648
[SPEAKER_02]: Starts with the elements, start with perception, then the space, and then the consciousness is the most refined one.

227
00:14:29,668 --> 00:14:31,309
[SPEAKER_02]: But again, it's always the same principle.

228
00:14:31,369 --> 00:14:40,991
[SPEAKER_02]: So, it's just, if you have the capacity to maintain this level of context, establishment and discernment to the point of your consciousness and infinite space, yeah, that's absolutely great.

229
00:14:41,831 --> 00:14:46,312
[SPEAKER_02]: But, the problem is, people already misconceived the starting point.

230
00:14:46,352 --> 00:14:50,893
[SPEAKER_02]: So, talking about everything else is just gonna be like, information about everything which will

231
00:14:51,932 --> 00:14:56,997
[SPEAKER_02]: Quite often, the result is, aha, okay, that's what this is, that's what this is, that's what this is, and you haven't established anything.

232
00:14:57,017 --> 00:14:58,779
[SPEAKER_02]: There's no right context established at all.

233
00:14:58,839 --> 00:15:05,005
[SPEAKER_02]: You're just having it all on the, like, abstract layout, and making sense of it over there.

234
00:15:11,793 --> 00:15:22,722
[SPEAKER_00]: So, all of these aspects, or all of these, I guess, consciousness, space, fire, water, they all share those same characteristics of just that imperturbability.

235
00:15:23,282 --> 00:15:24,623
[SPEAKER_02]: Well, they're not on the same plane.

236
00:15:25,244 --> 00:15:27,986
[SPEAKER_02]: So, it's not like these whole things share these characteristics.

237
00:15:28,926 --> 00:15:33,190
[SPEAKER_02]: For you, the first thing, the first framework, the first container is the solid.

238
00:15:33,970 --> 00:15:35,892
[SPEAKER_02]: Within the solid, you get to discern fluid.

239
00:15:36,152 --> 00:15:40,856
[SPEAKER_02]: Within the solid, within the fluid, you get to discern airy, and then within that, you get to discern fire.

240
00:15:42,573 --> 00:15:44,455
[SPEAKER_02]: Not left or right, or before or after it.

241
00:15:49,720 --> 00:15:50,320
[SPEAKER_02]: So, that's what I mean.

242
00:15:51,181 --> 00:16:04,314
[SPEAKER_02]: You want to resist the temptation to go into the abstract with figuring them all out, making sense of it, and actually focus on, okay, no, I'll just be patient, I'll put these other three aside, in the same sense with the jhānas, and develop the first.

243
00:16:06,441 --> 00:16:13,306
[SPEAKER_02]: Establish your mind upon the context of solidity that endures as a necessary basis for any experience that is currently occurring to you.

244
00:16:15,547 --> 00:16:17,208
[SPEAKER_02]: So, you don't know, I must stop this experience.

245
00:16:17,229 --> 00:16:18,589
[SPEAKER_02]: No, I must see beyond it.

246
00:16:18,649 --> 00:16:25,634
[SPEAKER_02]: I must see what is a necessary basis so that I can finally have space to not own this anymore.

247
00:16:25,654 --> 00:16:27,556
[SPEAKER_02]: You can't own it as an act of will.

248
00:16:27,776 --> 00:16:28,536
[SPEAKER_02]: Oh, this is not mine.

249
00:16:28,837 --> 00:16:29,557
[SPEAKER_02]: Well, that is yours.

250
00:16:30,458 --> 00:16:32,279
[SPEAKER_02]: Your denial of ownership is what you own.

251
00:16:33,482 --> 00:16:36,223
[SPEAKER_02]: But if you see that... whether you... oh, this is mine, this is not mine.

252
00:16:36,263 --> 00:16:38,263
[SPEAKER_02]: It's all undermining something that's inconceivably.

253
00:16:38,963 --> 00:16:40,323
[SPEAKER_02]: It's inconceivable to be yours.

254
00:16:40,543 --> 00:16:44,524
[SPEAKER_02]: You cannot possibly conceive container of earth that you can step outside of it and own it.

255
00:16:44,824 --> 00:16:46,465
[SPEAKER_02]: You can't even fantasize about it.

256
00:16:47,305 --> 00:16:53,186
[SPEAKER_02]: And when that becomes clear, any sense of ownership maintained within the dependence of that context, will have to fade.

257
00:16:53,586 --> 00:16:57,687
[SPEAKER_02]: It will not be the ownership, in the sense of I am the real genuine owner.

258
00:17:01,592 --> 00:17:05,395
[SPEAKER_02]: It's like the sutta says, you know, borrowed jewelry.

259
00:17:06,236 --> 00:17:09,099
[SPEAKER_02]: When you borrow the gold and jewelry and then you forget that you borrowed it.

260
00:17:10,340 --> 00:17:15,804
[SPEAKER_02]: And you're enjoying the pleasures you get on account of it, admiration you get on account of it, value you get on account of it.

261
00:17:16,385 --> 00:17:18,947
[SPEAKER_02]: And then, you know, the real owner comes and takes it away.

262
00:17:19,448 --> 00:17:22,470
[SPEAKER_02]: Because you completely lost perception that you never owned it.

263
00:17:22,630 --> 00:17:23,391
[SPEAKER_02]: It was only borrowed.

264
00:17:24,612 --> 00:17:27,374
[SPEAKER_02]: So you don't suffer because you borrowed it or because you lost it.

265
00:17:27,395 --> 00:17:28,976
[SPEAKER_02]: You suffer because you thought you owned it.

266
00:17:30,543 --> 00:17:37,266
[SPEAKER_02]: If you never forgot that it will have to be taken away, you will not be surprised when it's taken away, which means you can't suffer when it's taken away.

267
00:17:38,846 --> 00:17:41,087
[SPEAKER_02]: So, that's the whole point.

268
00:17:41,107 --> 00:17:50,931
[SPEAKER_02]: You want to undermine this gratuitous sense of ownership of your own body, of your own life, by seeing that it's owned by something much greater that you cannot even conceive owning.

269
00:17:51,692 --> 00:17:56,214
[SPEAKER_02]: And that's how you will remove any... any dependence on that body and that life.

270
00:17:58,415 --> 00:17:59,455
[SPEAKER_02]: So, you can still use it,

271
00:18:01,214 --> 00:18:08,376
[SPEAKER_02]: Like, you would borrow things, but that would not lead you to assume that you are the owner, master, controller, creator of those things.

272
00:18:09,137 --> 00:18:11,517
[SPEAKER_01]: I mean, that's kind of not optional.

273
00:18:11,577 --> 00:18:15,639
[SPEAKER_01]: That's part of the nature of having this body.

274
00:18:16,079 --> 00:18:16,479
[SPEAKER_01]: Which one?

275
00:18:16,819 --> 00:18:17,920
[SPEAKER_02]: That you have to use it.

276
00:18:18,080 --> 00:18:22,961
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah, that's why it automatically results in the view of attavāda and the ownership.

277
00:18:23,481 --> 00:18:25,502
[SPEAKER_02]: You don't need to, like, oh, now I need to develop the wrong view.

278
00:18:25,542 --> 00:18:25,642
[SPEAKER_02]: No.

279
00:18:25,682 --> 00:18:30,704
[SPEAKER_02]: Automatically, there is no beginning where the wrong view was not manifested beforehand.

280
00:18:31,391 --> 00:18:33,312
[SPEAKER_02]: But it shouldn't be there, because you were never the owner.

281
00:18:33,352 --> 00:18:34,373
[SPEAKER_02]: You could have never owned it.

282
00:18:34,793 --> 00:18:38,435
[SPEAKER_02]: But you don't know that, because of not knowing that, that's why you own it.

283
00:18:39,555 --> 00:18:44,818
[SPEAKER_02]: And that's why you're gonna get affected when those things do not obey your mastery, your ownership, your will.

284
00:18:46,019 --> 00:18:47,620
[SPEAKER_01]: When they don't go the way you want them to be.

285
00:18:50,081 --> 00:18:53,443
[SPEAKER_02]: But, unless you find out the way to uproot the ownership, you can't.

286
00:18:54,240 --> 00:18:58,286
[SPEAKER_02]: That's why it doesn't matter the amount of misfortune you might experience in life, the amount of loss.

287
00:18:59,047 --> 00:19:01,650
[SPEAKER_02]: You're still never going to abandon atavāda on account of it.

288
00:19:02,672 --> 00:19:03,433
[SPEAKER_02]: Because you don't know.

289
00:19:04,715 --> 00:19:05,416
[SPEAKER_02]: You don't know how.

290
00:19:06,397 --> 00:19:07,318
[SPEAKER_02]: You don't know what to see.

291
00:19:07,338 --> 00:19:08,920
[SPEAKER_02]: Because all you see is me and everything else.

292
00:19:09,842 --> 00:19:11,063
[SPEAKER_02]: That's all arahant sees as well.

293
00:19:11,773 --> 00:19:18,095
[SPEAKER_02]: But the difference is, Arhant puts everything else as a necessary container for me, which has now resulted in complete removal of ownership.

294
00:19:18,635 --> 00:19:23,016
[SPEAKER_02]: Gautujana doesn't put everything else as a necessary condition for me.

295
00:19:23,076 --> 00:19:23,916
[SPEAKER_01]: He puts it the other way around.

296
00:19:23,956 --> 00:19:24,876
[SPEAKER_01]: He puts himself first.

297
00:19:25,636 --> 00:19:26,077
[SPEAKER_02]: And that's it.

298
00:19:26,757 --> 00:19:31,818
[SPEAKER_02]: You can't change neither my point of view nor the world, but you can certainly change what is being prioritized.

299
00:19:32,258 --> 00:19:40,160
[SPEAKER_02]: That's so that the sense restraint in the Buddha would constantly, kind of, keep reiterating that you must not give in to desire and lust.

300
00:19:40,480 --> 00:19:44,024
[SPEAKER_02]: Because it's through that kind of engagement with the world, you maintain the wrong order.

301
00:19:44,685 --> 00:19:49,170
[SPEAKER_02]: By removing the desire and lust, by not acting out of it, you're at least not perpetuating the wrong order.

302
00:19:49,670 --> 00:19:50,711
[SPEAKER_02]: And then you get to understand it.

303
00:19:50,771 --> 00:19:53,654
[SPEAKER_02]: And when you do, then there is no more desire and lust even to arrive.

